WHAT IS BEING LICENSED, AND WHAT IS NOT

The numerical values in this repository are experimental measurements made
and published by the authors cited in SOURCES.md. They are facts about the
physical world, redistributed here as transcribed data with full attribution
to those authors. We do not claim ownership of anyone's measurements, and
users must cite the original experimental sources (SOURCES.bib) alongside
this dataset.

What the CC-BY-4.0 grant covers is the compilation: the transcription of the
printed tables, the unit conversions, the uniform schema, the quality coding,
the deduplication, and the provenance apparatus that ties each row to its
source.

No publisher PDF, and no part of the text or typography of any cited paper,
is included in this repository or is redistributable by us. SOURCES.md exists
so that it does not need to be: it gives a full reference, a DOI and a
resolvable URL for every source, so that any row can be checked against the
original obtained through the reader's own library.

